  "keyFeatures": [
    "Cross-platform local sockets backed by Unix domain sockets on Unix and named pipes on Windows",
    "Unnamed pipes for parent-child process communication",
    "FIFO files (Unix) for communicating with programs that expect named pipes",
    "Windows named pipes with full configuration including security descriptors",
    "Tokio async support for local sockets and unnamed pipes",
    "Stable, guaranteed name-to-primitive mapping for interoperability with non-Rust programs",
    "Peer credentials (PID, UID, GID) access on supported platforms",
    "Zero-overhead enum dispatch with platform-specific backends",
    "Filesystem path and abstract namespace name types (GenericFilePath, GenericNamespaced)",
    "Nonblocking mode, read/write timeouts, and stream splitting"
  ],
